#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: 8 lemons 22
#> pause: 40
#> must: 7 kiwis 18
#> must: 8 lemons 22
#> not: 6 grapes 40
#> not: 1 apples 12
#> source: $!D
# 3. P and D work on the first line of a multi-line pattern space. Sheet: "D" deletes
# up to the newline and restarts the commands without reading a new line.
# $!N appends the next line unless this is the last; $!D then drops the older of the
# two and goes round again. The pattern space is a two-line window that slides
# to the end of the input, where auto-print shows it: tail -2 in four characters.
# Try: $!N;P;D prints each line once; P prints only the first line of the window.
$!N
$!D

#DATA
1 apples 12
2 bananas 30
3 cherries 7
4 dates 16
5 figs 25
6 grapes 40
7 kiwis 18
8 lemons 22
